# Why I keep coming back to a personal assistant

I do not actually want a robot lifestyle.

What I want is to stop paying the same stupid attention tax over and over again.

Too much of my week is consumed by reloading context I already earned once. What did I promise that client, which school note mattered, why did I postpone that print, what exactly did Petra ask for, which half-finished product thought still feels true after three bad nights of sleep, what bit of operational pain at work is worth extracting into a real pattern instead of solving one more time with adrenaline and memory.

None of those are individually dramatic. Together they create the feeling that my life is made of open loops that keep breeding in the dark.


