# 112 lines
     1	<!-- AICODE-NOTE: Keep email-send semantics here, not scattered across outbox and finance docs. This file should define the reusable contract for draft-vs-sent state, recipient resolution, timestamped filenames, and attachment paths without leaking task-specific recipes. -->
     2	
     3	# Sending email
     4	
     5	Use this workflow for outbound email work: sending, drafting, replying, or resending.
     6	
     7	The workspace models outbound email as markdown files under `60_outbox/outbox/`.
     8	
     9	## Core rules
    10	
    11	- Resolve authority, lane, and recipient before writing any outbound email record.
    12	- If the request changes recipient, crosses lanes, touches money, or otherwise creates a new obligation, prefer clarification over guessing.
    13	- A known human name is not enough by itself. Use a visible verified address, preferably the relevant entity's `primary_contact_email`.
    14	- Prefer recipient choices that are already justified by visible canonical evidence.
    15	- Legacy email-channel docs are not the canonical source for recipient email addresses. Use them as context only.
    16	- Keep attachments as exact workspace paths. Do not invent external URLs or filesystem paths outside the visible repo.
    17	- Outbox files represent prepared communication state, not brainstorming.
    18	
    19	## File path
    20	
    21	Create outbound email records in `60_outbox/outbox/` using this filename format:
    22	
    23	```text
    24	eml_YYYY-MM-DDTHH-MM-SSZ.md
    25	```
    26	
    27	Timestamp rules:
    28	
    29	- derive the timestamp from the runtime-visible current time
    30	- use UTC `Z` form
    31	- replace `:` with `-` in the filename only
    32	- keep the frontmatter timestamp in normal RFC3339 form
    33	
    34	Example:
    35	
    36	```text
    37	60_outbox/outbox/eml_2026-04-10T09-30-00Z.md
    38	```
    39	
    40	## Frontmatter schema
    41	
    42	Write the email record as markdown with YAML frontmatter.
    43	
    44	```yaml
    45	---
    46	record_type: outbound_email
    47	created_at: 2026-04-10T09:30:00Z
    48	send_state: draft
    49	to:
    50	  - recipient@example.com
    51	subject: Follow-up
    52	attachments:
    53	  - 30_knowledge/notes/example.md
    54	related_entities:
    55	  - person.example
    56	related_projects:
    57	  - project.example
    58	source_channel: 60_outbox/channels/example.md
    59	---
    60	Hello,
    61	
    62	Following up with the requested note attached.
    63	
    64	Best,
    65	Miles
    66	```
    67	
    68	Required fields:
    69	
    70	- `record_type`
    71	- `created_at`
    72	- `send_state`
    73	- `to`
    74	- `subject`
    75	- `attachments`
    76	
    77	Optional fields:
    78	
    79	- `related_entities`
    80	- `related_projects`
    81	- `source_channel`
    82	
    83	Field rules:
    84	
    85	- `record_type` must be `outbound_email`
    86	- `created_at` must be the runtime-derived RFC3339 timestamp
    87	- `send_state` should be `draft` unless the visible workflow for this lane establishes a later state
    88	- `to` is an array of exact recipient email addresses
    89	- recipient email addresses should come from visible canonical entity email fields, especially `primary_contact_email`, when available
    90	- `subject` should be concrete and appropriate to the request
    91	- `attachments` is an array of exact workspace-relative file paths
    92	- for invoice resends or invoice bundles, order attachments reverse chronologically by the visible invoice issue date unless the request explicitly asks for something else; newest-first is the default because finance review usually starts with the latest invoice
    93	- `related_entities` and `related_projects` should use visible canonical ids when the relevant person or project has been resolved
    94	- `source_channel` should point to the visible channel doc when the email is a reply or lane-specific follow-up
    95	
    96	## Body rules
    97	
    98	- Put the email body below the frontmatter as normal markdown text.
    99	- Keep the draft narrow and purpose-built for the request.
   100	- Do not claim the email was already sent unless the visible workflow or request establishes sent state.
   101	- Mention only attachments that actually exist in the workspace.
   102	
   103	## Recipient resolution
   104	
   105	- For reply-shaped requests:
   106	  - prefer the recipient already established by the visible message context
   107	  - if the request comes from a structured inbox email record, use `processing-inbox-email.md` and treat that header as the canonical message metadata
   108	- For a request that names a recipient without a visible verified address:
   109	  - resolve it from canonical visible docs first
   110	  - if the visible docs do not identify one clear address, clarify instead of guessing
   111	- When an entity has a visible `primary_contact_email`, prefer that address over legacy email-channel material.
   112	- Do not silently switch to a new address mentioned in message text unless the workspace explicitly establishes that new address as trusted for that lane

